MEMORY(1)         KERNEL MEMORY ALLOCATION FUNCTIONS           MEMORY(1)NAME       memory - kernel dynamic memory allocationSYNOPSIS       memory ( -- )       malloc ( bytes -- ptr)       realloc ( bytes ptr -- ptr)       free ( ptr -- )DESCRIPTION       Kernel support for dynamic memory allocation from the run-time       heap.memory ( -- )       Vocabulary containing the heap management extension.malloc ( bytes -- ptr)       Allocates "bytes" and returns a pointer to the memory area.       Returns nil if the heap is saturated.realloc ( bytes ptr -- ptr)       Resizes an allocated block on the heap. If the new size is       larger than the grow size of the block. A new block is       allocated and the old blocks contains is copied and freed.      free ( ptr -- )       Returns a block of memory to the heap pool.SEE ALSO       forth(1)WARNING       Code written using this word set is not directly portable to       other forth environments.BUG       Pointers are not check. Illegal pointer value will result in       a possible error situation.     COPYING       Copyright (C) 1989 Mikael R.K. Patel       Permission is granted to make and distribute verbatim copies       of this manual provided the copyright notice and this permission       notice are preserved on all copies.       Permission is granted to copy and distribute modified versions       of this manual under the conditions for verbatim copying,        provided also that the section entitled "GNU General Public       License" is included exactly as in the original, and provided       that the entire resulting derived work is distributed under       the terms of a permission notice identical to this one.       Permission is granted to copy and distribute translations of       this manual into another language, under the above conditions       for modified versions, except that the section entitled "GNU       General Public License" may be included in a tran